20: /* IOEventSource implementation used as the bridge's event sink.
21:  *
22:  * Producer context: copy a bounded event record under an interrupt-safe spin
23:  * lock, then signalWorkAvailable(). No allocation, sleeping, Apple message
24:  * posting or radio calls occur on this path.
25:  *
26:  * Consumer context: IOWorkLoop calls checkForWork(), which drains the ring and
27:  * invokes the handler on the controller's work-loop thread.
28:  *
29:  * Lifecycle contract: detach and quiesce the RTW88 bridge before stop/free.
30:  * stop() must run outside this event source's active checkForWork()/handler
31:  * callback; IOWorkLoop removal serializes against any in-flight work check.
